# On the live host the API subdomain's web root is THIS folder (the one holding
# artisan and .env), not public/. Without this file the API only answers under
# /public/..., and composer.json, artisan and the rest of the source can be
# downloaded by anyone.
#
# Every request is handed to public/, where Laravel's own .htaccess and
# index.php take over — exactly as if the subdomain pointed at public/.
# Harmless when it already does: then this folder is never served.
<IfModule mod_rewrite.c>
    RewriteEngine On
    RewriteRule ^(.*)$ public/$1 [L]
</IfModule>
